{{!-- The head every GM-prep card wears: the accent edge, the host's collapse chrome, and the
      title/type pair. Shared by the threat, hazard and site cards, which is what lets one set of
      handlers drive all three (StonetopSteadingSheet._activateThreatsListeners binds
      `.threat-card__head--collapsible` and `.threat-collapse-btn` once, for every kind).

      The card's <article> wrapper stays with each card, because that is where the three genuinely
      differ — its modifier class and its `data-<kind>-id`, which is what the steading sheet reads
      a card's kind back off.

      Context: the card's own view-model, plus
        `kind`      the noun the collapse button's aria-label uses ("threat", "hazard", "site")
        `typeLabel` what this card calls itself in the header ("Hazard", a threat's type label) --}}
<span class="threat-card__edge" aria-hidden="true"></span>

<header class="threat-card__head{{#if collapsible}} threat-card__head--collapsible{{/if}}">
	{{#if collapsible}}
	{{!-- Host-added collapse chrome (the steading's prep tabs only): clamps the card to its
	      title + Instinct. The chevron reflects/announces state; clicking anywhere on the header
	      toggles it. --}}
	<button type="button" class="threat-collapse-btn"
	        aria-expanded="{{#if collapsed}}false{{else}}true{{/if}}"
	        aria-label="Collapse or expand this {{kind}}" tabindex="0">
		<i class="fas fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"></i>
	</button>
	{{/if}}
	<div class="threat-card__title">
		<h3 class="threat-name">{{name}}</h3>
		<span class="threat-type">{{typeLabel}}</span>
	</div>
</header>
